From 98a7535d22304023ed321e1b973ec8d435d9683e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 18:20:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/75] Suppress activity relaunch on screenSize for resizable
 activities
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ARC apps are dragged across physical displays with different DSFs;
each crossover changes the window's effective screen-size config.
For activities whose manifest doesn't list screenSize in
android:configChanges (e.g. com.android.settings.Settings, most AOSP
apps), Android's default response is to destroy + recreate the
activity, which produces a visible reset/flash and resets the window
to the activity's freeform default — undoing whatever size the user
had before.

Most modern apps are responsive enough to handle screen-size changes
in-process without breaking; they just don't bother to declare it.
For any activity that's already opted into resizing
(android:resizeableActivity != false → isResizeable() returns true),
treat CONFIG_SCREEN_SIZE | CONFIG_SMALLEST_SCREEN_SIZE |
CONFIG_SCREEN_LAYOUT as implicitly handled in
ActivityRecord.shouldRelaunchLocked(). Activities that genuinely
can't handle resize have already opted out via
android:resizeableActivity="false" and won't take this path.

Change-Id: If188e1315460f76d2decfeec3b2bf1bdf8d29e47
---
 .../com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java  | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
index 6325a5a05dd5..8788b611b843 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/ActivityRecord.java
@@ -9515,6 +9515,24 @@ final class ActivityRecord extends WindowToken implements WindowManagerService.A
             configChanged |= CONFIG_UI_MODE;
         }
 
+        // fydroid-rt: assume any resizable activity implicitly handles
+        // screen-size config changes, even if its manifest doesn't list
+        // them in android:configChanges. Many AOSP apps (Settings,
+        // PackageInstaller, etc.) are responsive enough to handle
+        // size changes without breaking, but they don't bother to
+        // declare it — and our Wayland window crossover keeps producing
+        // size-change events that flash the user with destroy/create
+        // cycles. Suppressing the relaunch lets these apps retain
+        // state and avoid the visible reset; activities that genuinely
+        // can't handle resize have already opted out via
+        // android:resizeableActivity="false" (which makes isResizeable()
+        // return false).
+        if (isResizeable()) {
+            configChanged |= CONFIG_SCREEN_SIZE
+                    | CONFIG_SMALLEST_SCREEN_SIZE
+                    | CONFIG_SCREEN_LAYOUT;
+        }
+
         return (changes & (~configChanged)) != 0;
     }
 
